   "evidence": "At HEAD, engine.ts:1859 marks a local finder with `...(finder?.local ? { billing: \"free_only\" as const } : {})`, but lines 1840\u20131843 attach checkout whenever `ctx.repo.kind === \"github\" && ctx.run.branch`. context.ts:545 obtains the pinned chain from `this.run.models?.[opts.role as RunRole]` and passes it to routing. router.ts:379\u2013380 uses `const paid = !c.chain && c.billing !== undefined && m.billing !== \"free\" ? 1 : 0; if (paid && c.billing === \"free_only\") continue;`, so a pinned subscription target survives. lan-agent.ts:26\u201340 then accepts the readonly review with checkout and no credential-bearing target fields. At base, the routing behavior already existed, but the review call supplied no checkout and the executor accepted only publishing implement calls; the worker dispatch defect is introduced by this change."
